# Parrot recording v2
# GENERATED by generate.py. Do not edit. Change the generator and rerun it.
#
# Replay overhead benchmark, measured phase: 50 pointer moves per second.
#
# 3000 mousemove events, 20 ms apart, for 60 s. The pointer alternates between
# 560,380 and 880,500, both inside the xlogo window. xlogo draws nothing on
# pointer motion, so the application's share of a move is nil and the X
# server's share is the same for both injectors. The rest is the injector.
#
# The wait comes FIRST inside the loop body. `loop` clears the pending wait
# when it jumps, so a wait written just before the `loop` line would be
# dropped on every iteration but the last.

startcommand = xlogo
windowtitle = xlogo
windowclass = xlogo

log Mousemove 50 Hz: 3000 pointer moves, 20 ms apart, for 60 s
label move
wait 0.020000
mousemove 560 380
wait 0.020000
mousemove 880 500
loop move 1500
log Mousemove 50 Hz complete: 3000 pointer moves in 60 s of recorded time
